 INPUT CARD>! point from caa005bTSa.log ("***** SADDLE POINT LOCATED *****"), which         
 INPUT CARD>! was itself confirmed genuine at the original level (wB97X-D, GBASIS=N21       
 INPUT CARD>! NGAUSS=6 NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.T., i.e. a 3-21G-family basis with diffuse and      
 INPUT CARD>! polarization functions, not the same as the IRC path's 6-31G(d)-style         
 INPUT CARD>! basis, but same functional): EXACTLY ONE imaginary frequency (1156.17i),      
 INPUT CARD>! all other modes real. That original search used an explicitly supplied        
 INPUT CARD>! starting Hessian ($HESS ... READ). We do not have an equivalent Hessian       
 INPUT CARD>! for this new basis, so this run instead relies on IHREP=1 (a genuinely        
 INPUT CARD>! fresh Hessian recomputed every step) plus GAMESS's default mode-following     
 INPUT CARD>! (IFOLOW=1) to track the correct transition mode -- the same approach that     
 INPUT CARD>! has already worked reliably for caa007a/caa007b's minimizations.              
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! RUNTYP=SADPOINT (NOT OPTIMIZE) -- this searches for a first-order saddle      
 INPUT CARD>! point rather than a minimum, essential for a TS. Using OPTIMIZE here          
 INPUT CARD>! would simply relax the structure down into a nearby minimum, losing the       
 INPUT CARD>! transition state entirely.                                                    
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! NOTE: first submission attempt omitted an explicit HESS= setting in           
 INPUT CARD>! $STATPT. Unlike RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE (which defaults to HESS=GUESS),               
 INPUT CARD>! RUNTYP=SADPOINT defaults to HESS=READ, expecting an explicit $HESS group      
 INPUT CARD>! -- which we don't have for this basis. GAMESS aborted immediately with        
 INPUT CARD>! "YOU DID NOT SUPPLY A $HESS GROUP." Fixed by explicitly setting               
 INPUT CARD>! HESS=GUESS, overriding that default; IHREP=1 (fresh Hessian every step)       
 INPUT CARD>! should correct for the guess's lower quality quickly, the same way it         
 INPUT CARD>! did for caa007a/caa007b's minimizations.                                      
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! NOTE (final): switched strategy entirely rather than keep fighting the        
 INPUT CARD>! HESS=GUESS override (see caa005bTSb-hess.inp). Computed a genuine Hessian     
 INPUT CARD>! via a standalone RUNTYP=HESSIAN run at this exact geometry/level, then        
 INPUT CARD>! extracted the PROJECTED Hessian block (translation/rotation removed,          
 INPUT CARD>! matching PROJCT=.T.) from caa005bTSb-hess.dat -- confirmed by the             
 INPUT CARD>! "----- HESSIAN MATRIX AFTER PROJECTION -----" label immediately preceding     
 INPUT CARD>! it in the punch file, distinguishing it from the earlier raw/unprojected      
 INPUT CARD>! $HESS block. That block is appended below and HESS is set to READ             
 INPUT CARD>! (GAMESS's own default for SADPOINT), working with the program rather          
 INPUT CARD>! than against it.                                                              
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
