 INPUT CARD>! "NOT 5 OR 6 TRANS/ROT MODES, NUM T/R=7" -- one spurious extra near-zero       
 INPUT CARD>! eigenvalue beyond the expected 6, most likely from this run's own             
 INPUT CARD>! PROJCT=.T. re-projecting an already-projected Hessian (double                 
 INPUT CARD>! projection). Checked directly in GAMESS's source (statpt.src): the            
 INPUT CARD>! trans/rot count comes from counting eigenvalues below a small tolerance       
 INPUT CARD>! (TRTOL), and the check (hardcoded N5OR6=5, tolerating up to N5OR6+1=6         
